Here's a Java code that calculates the maximum value in an array, along with its indices, without using any built-in functions or libraries:

```java
public class MaximumValueWithIndices {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] array = {5, 2, 7, -2, 10, 7, -2, 7};
        int[] maxIndices = findMaximumValueWithIndices(array);

        System.out.println("Maximum value: " + array[maxIndices[0]]);
        System.out.print("Indices: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < maxIndices.length; i++) {
            System.out.print(maxIndices[i] + " ");
        }
    }

    public static int[] findMaximumValueWithIndices(int[] array) {
        int max = array[0];
        int[] indices = new int[array.length];
        int count = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < array.length; i++) {
            if (array[i] > max) {
                max = array[i];
                count = 0;
            }
            if (array[i] == max) {
                indices[count] = i;
                count++;
            }
        }

        int[] result = new int[count + 1];
        result[0] = max;
        for (int i = 1; i < result.length; i++) {
            result[i] = indices[i - 1];
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

